class:: AttackSlope2
summary:: Externally triggered attack slope
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Slope

description::
A positive trigger edge begins a fixed maxTime capture of nonoverlapping RMS envelope frames. A new trigger restarts an unfinished capture. After capture, the largest RMS peak defines relative lowRatio and highRatio thresholds. The attack runs from the first upward low crossing to the first upward high crossing before the peak; decay runs from the first downward high crossing after the peak to the first downward low crossing. Linear interpolation refines crossing times between envelope frames. Attack slope is peak*(highRatio-lowRatio)/attackTime. These are independent, externally segmented event measurements: onset detection is supplied by the caller. The output holds the last completed result while a new capture runs. The first result arrives after maxTime, resolution is limited by frameTime, and events crossing the capture boundaries can be truncated. An already-high first frame has no observable rise. CPU is O(maxTime/frameTime) once per completed capture and memory is fixed at construction. The convention follows relative-threshold envelope attack descriptors, with explicit segmentation and crossing definitions.

Vanilla Slope differentiates a control stream; this UGen measures an entire captured attack or decay interval.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal whose event envelope is measured.

argument:: trigger
Positive edge at audio or control rate; starts or restarts capture. Zero by default, so supply a trigger.

argument:: maxTime
Literal capture time, 2*frameTime..10 seconds. Default 0.5.

argument:: frameTime
Literal RMS frame duration, 0.001..0.1 seconds. Default 0.005.

argument:: lowRatio
Relative peak threshold, clipped to 0.001..0.98; default 0.1.

argument:: highRatio
Relative peak threshold, clipped above lowRatio through 0.999; default 0.9.

returns::
RMS amplitude units per second; zero for an unresolved or instantaneous attack.

examples::
AttackSlope2 measures the linear rise slope (peak * (highRatio - lowRatio) / attackTime) of a captured transient event. Steep slopes indicate hard, forceful plucks or strikes; gentle slopes indicate soft legato playing. In this example, attack slope triggers a punchy sub-bass ping that reinforces hard-plucked notes. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: displays real-time attack slope.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("plucks.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic pluck fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(1.5);
            var env = EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.4), trig);
            Pluck.ar(WhiteNoise.ar * env, trig, 0.2, 1/220, 2.0, 0.3)
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var trig = Impulse.kr(1.5);
        var slope = AttackSlope2.kr(source, trig, maxTime: 0.5, frameTime: 0.005);
        var slopeLag = slope.lag(0.05);
        var punchTrig = (slopeLag > 2.0).lag(0.01, 0.08);
        var punch = SinOsc.ar(60, 0, punchTrig * 0.3);
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + (punch ! 2);

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, slopeLag.clip(0, 10)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Attack Slope", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 10.0, "slope");
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

